===Etymology 2===
* Noun: from {{inh|en|enm|sownde}}, alteration of {{m|enm|soun}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|sun}}, {{m|xno|soun}}, {{der|en|fro|son}}, from accusative of {{der|en|la|sonus}}, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*swenh₂-||to sound, resound}}.
* Verb: from {{inh|en|enm|sownden}}, {{m|enm|sounen}}, borrowed from {{der|en|xno|suner}}, {{m|fro|sounder}}, {{der|en|fro|soner}} (modern {{m|fr|sonner}}), from {{der|en|la|sonō}}.
* The hypercorrect '''-d''' appears in the fifteenth century. (Compare dialectal {{m|en|drownd|drown'''d'''}}, {{m|en|gownd|gown'''d'''}} for the same development.)
Displaced native {{ncog|enm|swei}}, from {{ncog|ang|swēġ}}, from {{ncog|gem-pro|*swōgiz}}.
{{wikipedia}}

