====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} Of a [[whale]], to [[dive]] downwards.
#: {{ux|en|The whale '''sounded''' and eight hundred feet of heavy line streaked out of the line tub before he ended his dive.}}
# To [[ascertain]], or to try to ascertain, the thoughts, motives, and purposes of (a person); to examine; to try; to test; to probe.
#: {{ux|en|When I '''sounded''' him, he appeared to favor the proposed deal.}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 2|I|i|23|1|Tell me moreouer, haſt thou '''ſounded''' him,/If he appeale the Duke on ancient malice,/Or worthily as a good ſubiect ſhould/On ſome knowne ground of treacherie in him.}}
