#* {{RQ:Addison Cato|1|1|passage=I've '''sounded''' my Numidians man by man.}}
# To [[fathom]] or [[test]]; to ascertain the depth of water with a sounding line or other device.
#: {{ux|en|Mariners on sailing ships would '''sound''' the depth of the water with a weighted rope.}}
#* {{RQ:Marlowe Tamburlaine|part=1|scene=ii|page=46|passage=As when the Sea-man {{...}}/All fearefull foldes his ſailes, and '''ſounds''' the maine,/Lifting his prayers to the heauens for aid,/Againſt the terrour of the winds and waues.}}
# {{lb|en|medicine}} To [[examine]] with the instrument called a sound or sonde, or by [[auscultation]] or [[percussion]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''sound''' a patient, or the bladder or urethra}}

