# {{lb|en|medicine}} A long, thin [[probe]] for [[sound#Verb|sounding]] or dilating body cavities or canals such as the urethra; a [[sonde]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|year=1951|month=January|author=Gordon W. Reynolds|title=The Female Urethra and Chronic Urethritis|journal=Northwest Medicine|volume=50|issue=1|location=Portland, Ore.|publisher=Northwest Medical Publishing Association|page=34|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/northwestmedicin5019nort/page/34/mode/2up?q=sounds|passage=Most mild cases respond very nicely to such relatively simple office procedures as dilatations with '''sounds''' of increasing calibre, followed by the instillation of an ounce of 5 per cent argyrol in the bladder.}}

